&lt;li&gt;Help define and drive Figma’s corporate storytelling strategy end-to-end, from narrative development to execution across channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move beyond traditional PR to create integrated campaigns that cut through across media, owned platforms and executive communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to translate business momentum into clear, compelling stories and campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with executives to shape narratives that resonate with business and financial audiences, from briefings to thought leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop breakthrough story angles that position Figma at the center of key industry, market and cultural conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the news cycle and broader zeitgeist while proactively creating opportunities that put Figma ahead of it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue to grow your scope and influence as the company scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in in-house communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and scaling communications programs from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business and cultural fluency, with the ability to translate complexity into clear, engaging narratives and pitches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in fast-paced environments where direction isn’t always defined—and comfort creating it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience crafting a point of view on storytelling that goes beyond conventional PR approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
